Automating Jenkins with REST API
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Install and configure Jenkins on a Linux machine
Understand the Jenkins REST API architecture and authentication methods
Create Jenkins jobs programmatically using REST API calls
Trigger builds automatically through API endpoints and retrieve build status via REST API
Update, verify, and safely delete Jenkins jobs through API automation
Build a reusable shell-based test suite to validate an end-to-end API automation workflow
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
Basic knowledge of JSON data format
Understanding of REST API concepts
Experience with the curl command-line tool
Basic shell scripting knowledge
Familiarity with CI/CD concepts
Required tools installed during the lab (commands provided in Task 1):

sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y openjdk-11-jdk curl jq
